From bb4f73317f0731df0699f7cecface2501c35645d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: orlfman <25542856+orlfman@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:25:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 10/16] linux: add Intel iGPU meters

Add meters for the Arrow Lake iGPU (i915, 8086:7d67): a heading
("Intel iGPU", with sleep and access states), render + compute
utilization, the requested GT0 clock, approximate allocated system
memory, and combined video encode/decode. Activity and memory come from
the DRM fdinfo of readable processes, so they cover visible clients
only; the meter descriptions say so.

The device is found from sysfs metadata only, without opening a DRM
node. Clients are counted once even when shared between processes or
file descriptors, per-client engine deltas need a baseline, and PID,
start time and fd ownership survives access gaps so lost access shows
as unavailable rather than as zero (AUDIT.md finding 8). Suspended,
rebound and unreadable devices are handled, memory units are checked,
and the clock limit is read on every refresh.

INTELGPU_SYSFS_ROOT and INTELGPU_PROC_ROOT allow pointing the sampler
at fake trees for testing.

Written by Codex; reviewed by Claude Code.

Co-Authored-By: OpenAI Codex (GPT-6) <noreply@openai.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
